@startuml
title Factory Scenario Description - Multi-Machine Predictive Maintenance

skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam defaultFontColor #1F2937
skinparam rectangleBorderColor #374151
skinparam rectangleBackgroundColor #F9FAFB
skinparam nodeBorderColor #2563EB
skinparam nodeBackgroundColor #EFF6FF
skinparam cloudBorderColor #7C3AED
skinparam cloudBackgroundColor #F5F3FF
skinparam databaseBorderColor #059669
skinparam databaseBackgroundColor #ECFDF5
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #FEF3C7
skinparam noteBorderColor #D97706
skinparam arrowColor #374151

left to right direction

note as Purpose
  Purpose:
  Defines the project's factory use case in a visual form.
  A small factory floor monitors multiple machine types using
  one ESP32 sensor node per machine, then sends machine health
  telemetry to a gateway/cloud for alerts and maintenance decisions.
end note

actor "Maintenance\nOperator" as Operator

rectangle "Factory Floor Scenario" as Factory {
  node "Machine 1\nCNC motor" as M1 {
    component "Temp sensor" as M1T
    component "Vibration sensor" as M1V
    node "ESP32 Node M1" as E1
  }

  node "Machine 2\nConveyor motor" as M2 {
    component "Temp sensor" as M2T
    component "Vibration sensor" as M2V
    node "ESP32 Node M2" as E2
  }

  node "Machine 3\nCompressor" as M3 {
    component "Temp sensor" as M3T
    component "Vibration sensor" as M3V
    node "ESP32 Node M3" as E3
  }
}

cloud "Factory Wi-Fi" as Wifi
node "Gateway / MQTT Broker" as Gateway
database "Cloud / Server\nTelemetry + Alerts + Trends" as CloudStore
component "Dashboard / Report" as Dashboard

M1T --> E1 : short wired link
M1V --> E1 : short wired link
M2T --> E2 : short wired link
M2V --> E2 : short wired link
M3T --> E3 : short wired link
M3V --> E3 : short wired link

E1 --> Wifi : MQTT telemetry\nmachineId=M1
E2 --> Wifi : MQTT telemetry\nmachineId=M2
E3 --> Wifi : MQTT telemetry\nmachineId=M3

Wifi --> Gateway : publish telemetry topics
Gateway --> CloudStore : store time-series records
CloudStore --> Dashboard : status, trends, KPIs
Dashboard --> Operator : alerts and maintenance view
Operator --> Dashboard : acknowledge / inspect

Gateway --> Wifi : alert topic per machine
Wifi --> E1 : alert/command if needed
Wifi --> E2 : alert/command if needed
Wifi --> E3 : alert/command if needed

legend bottom
|= Element |= Meaning |
| Machine 1..3 | Example factory assets monitored independently |
| Temp + vibration sensors | Physical measurements attached to each machine |
| ESP32 Node | Local edge device placed near one machine |
| MQTT telemetry | Machine data sent upstream using Wi-Fi |
| Alert topic | Message path from gateway/cloud back to the selected ESP32 |
| Operator | Human user who reviews alerts and plans maintenance |
endlegend
@enduml
